%% end

## 2. Answer the question

Use [scenarios](references/scenarios.md) ([中文](references/scenarios.zh-CN.md)) to:

- pick the skill for the user's situation;
- explain which models play each role and how to change them;
- answer common questions.

Keep the answer to what the user asked; offer the rest.

## 3. Offer a guided first run

When the user is new, offer a small, safe first run in the current repo: a read-only research task through `native-routed-{host}`, for example "explain how <some module> works and where its tests are". Walk through what happens as it happens: model resolution, the notes directory and `session.json`, the worker dispatch, acceptance. Afterwards show where the notes ended up.

Only run it when the user agrees; it starts real subagents that cost tokens.
